@baseUrl = http://localhost:7015/api/v1
@authToken = paste-a-token-from-auth.http-here

### Submit generic feedback (text only; images is optional and carries
### { data: "<base64>", mimeType } pairs -- the frontend reads each
### attached/pasted file as base64 and sends it inline, no upload step)
POST {{baseUrl}}/l1-feedback/generic HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Body pixel ratio to face pixel ratio must always be 7.5.",
  "images": [],
  "createdBy": "qa@flixstock.com"
}

### Submit a generation-bundle ZIP (metadata.json + outputs/*.jpg) -- this
### is a multipart/form-data request; the VS Code REST Client extension
### supports this natively, but plain copy-paste of this file into another
### HTTP client may not render the boundary correctly.
POST {{baseUrl}}/l1-feedback/generic/zip HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary123

------boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="text"

The poses in this bundle look wrong -- check the posing rules.
------boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="bundle"; filename="render.zip"
Content-Type: application/zip

< ./path/to/vertex_bundle.zip
------boundary123--

### List generic feedback requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/l1-feedback/generic HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Get one generic feedback request (poll while status is "processing")
GET {{baseUrl}}/l1-feedback/generic/{{genericFeedbackId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Approve candidate_0 on target 0
POST {{baseUrl}}/l1-feedback/generic/{{genericFeedbackId}}/decision HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "targetIndex": 0,
  "decision": "candidate_0",
  "comment": "Agreed, matches the intended ratio.",
  "decidedBy": "qa@flixstock.com"
}

### Delete a generic feedback request (e.g. a test/junk submission)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/l1-feedback/generic/{{genericFeedbackId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
